  "description": "Our Sgt. Mingo model is named after one of the leaders of the US Army’s 25th Infantry Bicycle Corps. This was the first regiment equipped with bicycles and was also one of the first African-American military units. In 1897 Sgt. Mingo led his unit on a grueling 1,900 mile trek entirely on bicycles from Missoula, Montana to St. Louis Missouri. As first sergeant he was considered the motivator and inspiration of the group.\n\nThe Mingo is a sturdy, mountain bike style frame. Designed for maximum fun the Sgt. Mingo is our ‘go anywhere, do anything’ model. Performance driven styling and the innovative frame design makes this perfect for the urban commuter. We think Sgt. Mingo would have been proud!",
